  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "A wooden crate of mass $14\\,\\text{kg}$ falls vertically downward. Let $v$ be its velocity, with downward taken as the positive direction.\nThe air resistance on the crate is proportional to its velocity and acts in the opposite direction to the motion.\nAt a particular moment during the fall, the crate\u2019s velocity is $7\\,\\text{m/s}$ and its instantaneous acceleration is $6.3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhat is the terminal velocity ${v}_{\\text{term}}$ of the crate? Assume the acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ and the only forces acting on the crate are the weight due to gravity and drag.\n\n${v}_{\\text{term}}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}$",
  "worked_solution": "Terminal velocity is the constant speed a falling object approaches as the upward resistive force (drag) grows to exactly balance the downward gravitational force.\nThat is, at terminal velocity (a constant), acceleration is zero, so by $F=ma,$ the resultant force is zero.\n\nFirst, note that only two forces act on the crate: the force due to gravity, given by the weight\n\n$$\nw=mg=14\\cdot 9.8=137.2\\,\\text{N},\n$$\n\nand the force due to drag $D,$ which is proportional to the velocity (and negative since it acts in the negative direction),\n\n$$\nD=-kv,\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Hence, the resultant force acting on the crate is\n\n$$\nF=w+D=137.2-kv.\n$$\n\nApplying Newton's second law, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\ 137.2-kv & =14a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that, at a particular moment, the crate\u2019s velocity is $7\\,\\text{m/s}$ and its instantaneous acceleration is $6.3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Substituting these values into the above, we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}137.2-7k & =14\\cdot 6.3 \\\\ 137.2-7k & =88.2 \\\\ -7k & =-49 \\\\ k & =7\\,\\text{kg/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the resultant force acting on the crate is\n\n$$\nF=137.2-7v.\n$$\n\nWhen the crate reaches terminal velocity ${v}_{\\text{term}},$ the resultant force is zero:\n\n$$\n137.2-7{v}_{\\text{term}}=0\\,\u27f9\\,{v}_{\\text{term}}=\\frac{137.2}{7}=19.6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the terminal velocity of the crate is ${v}_{\\text{term}}=19.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
